e_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "James and Mary have a date at the cinema theater.\nJames arrived at the agreed time, but Mary is late. After $20$ minutes of waiting, James decides to go home.\n\nJames travels north from the theater with a speed of $3.2\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Mary travels west toward the theater. When James is $0.8\\,\\text{km}$ from the theater, Mary is $1.5\\,\\text{km}$ from the theater. If the distance between them increases at a speed of $2.3\\,\\text{km/h},$ what is Mary's speed?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by drawing a diagram of the problem.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/assets/1728c9ca91ef28b19c28048f5a640d0eebbd08f504bb594bc978277fe5620d70.png)\n\nIn the diagram,\n\n- $x$ is the distance between Mary and the cinema theater,\n\n- $y$ is the distance between James and the cinema theater,\n\n- $z$ is the distance between James and Mary.\n\nAs shown in the diagram, $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ form a right triangle with $z$ as the hypotenuse. We wish to find the rate of change of $x,$ which is $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ \n\nWe know that $x=1.5\\,\\text{km}$ and $y=0.8\\,\\text{km}.$ We can find $z$ using the Pythagorean Theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {1.5}^{2}+{0.8}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =2.89 \\\\ z & =1.7\\,\\text{km}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that:\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3.2\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h},$\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}=2.3\\,\\text{km}/\\text{h}.$\n\nFinally, we differentiate both sides of ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and then substitute in the known values, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({z}^{2}) \\\\ 2x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 2(1.5)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(0.8)(3.2) & =2(1.7)(2.3) \\\\ 3\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =7.82-5.12 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mary is approaching the cinema theater with a speed of $0.9\\,\\text{km/h}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "156e1ba9a0f022ec478436db5102f8eea38de4f3485accd29c129b1d286402b2" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103792" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103792" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.7\\,\\text{km/h}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103792" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.8\\,\\text{km/h}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103792" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.9\\,\\text{km/h}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103792" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.1\\,\\text{km/h}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103792" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1\\,\\text{km/h}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103792" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.9\\,\\text{km/h}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Alex and Brooke agree to meet at the library. Alex arrives on time, but Brooke is late. After waiting for a while, Alex decides to leave and calls Brooke. They agree to head home instead.\n\nAlex travels north from the library at a speed of $6\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Brooke travels east away from the library. When Alex is $4\\,\\text{km}$ from the library, Brooke is $3\\,\\text{km}$ from the library. If the distance between them is increasing at a rate of $6\\,\\text{km/h},$ what is Brooke’s speed?\n\nBrooke’s speed is \n{{field-1}}$\\text{ }\\text{km/h}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by drawing a diagram of the problem.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/assets/46263b1e25bc520881d590ccab503ce0d6cd33e91288e81f1d678cde9a641214.png)\n\nIn the diagram,\n\n- $x$ is the distance between Brooke and the library,\n\n- $y$ is the distance between Alex and the library,\n\n- $z$ is the distance between Alex and Brooke.\n\nAs shown in the diagram, $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ form a right triangle with $z$ as the hypotenuse. We wish to find the rate of change of $x,$ which is $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nWe know that $x=3\\,\\text{km}$ and $y=4\\,\\text{km}.$ We can find $z$ using the Pythagorean Theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {3}^{2}+{4}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 9+16 & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =25 \\\\ z & =5\\,\\text{km}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that:\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=6\\,\\text{km/h},$\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}=5\\,\\text{km/h}.$\n\nFinally, we differentiate both sides of ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and then substitute in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({z}^{2}) \\\\ 2x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2z\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 2(3)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(4)(6) & =2(5)(6) \\\\ 6\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+48 & =60 \\\\ 6\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Brooke's speed is $2\\,\\text{km/h}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "156e1ba9a0f022ec478436db5102f8eea38de4f3485accd29c129b1d286402b2" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-345644" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The length of one leg of a right triangle increases at the rate of $5\\text{ m/s},$ while the length of the second leg is decreasing at the rate of $3\\text{ m/s}.$ How fast is the length of the hypotenuse changing when the length of the increasing leg is $9\\text{ m}$ and the length of the decreasing leg is $12\\text{ m}?$\n\nThe length of the hypotenuse is changing at a rate of\n{{field-1}} $\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by drawing a diagram of the problem.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/assets/40fd26817dc71b5ceee1861e20a812a1835fdb92d0ff7a903d05aacc2eca2c05.png)\n\nIn the diagram,\n\n- $x$ is the length of the increasing side,\n\n- $y$ is the length of the decreasing side,\n\n- $z$ is the length of the hypotenuse.\n\nAs shown in the diagram, $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ form a right triangle with $z$ as the hypotenuse. We wish to find the rate of change of $z,$ which is $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nWe know that $x=9\\,\\text{m}$ and $y=12\\,\\text{m}.$ We can find $z$ using the Pythagorean Theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {9}^{2}+{12}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 225 & ={z}^{2} \\\\ z & =15\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that:\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=5\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $x=9\\,\\text{m}$ and $y=12\\,\\text{m},$\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=-3\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $x=9\\,\\text{m}$ and $y=12\\,\\text{m}.$\n\nFinally, we differentiate both sides of ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ with respect to $t$ and then substitute in the known values, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(9)(5)+2(12)(-3) & =2(15)\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 18 & =30\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the hypotenuse is changing at a rate of $\\frac{3}{5}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/state.json" "file_sha256" "89afe13b54736576b0a57d365fdf55ba97440adc5da071877637060a6634148b" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069977/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "156e1ba9a0f022ec478436db5102f8eea38de4f3485accd29c129b1d286402b2" "basis" 2445 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/ques